  "worked_solution": "The Cartesian equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, to write the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to divide both sides of the equation by $14$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =14 \\\\ \\frac{2{y}^{2}}{14}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{14} & =\\frac{14}{14} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{7}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{14} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
